  "hints": [
    "Think about the score margin the current player can force on an interval.",
    "After choosing an end, the opponent owns the next interval, so subtract their optimal margin.",
    "Cache margin(l,r)=max(nums[l]-margin(l+1,r), nums[r]-margin(l,r-1)); one remaining value is the base case.",
    "Player 1 succeeds exactly when the starting margin is nonnegative. Memoization collapses repeated game-tree intervals to O(n^2) states."
  ],
  "editorial": "The recursive margin is measured from the player whose turn it is, so changing turns reverses the sign. Caching intervals explores both strategic choices without exponential repetition. The independent oracle enumerates a literal alternating game tree, maximizing player-1 score on their turns and minimizing it on player-2 turns.",
